Compton camera simulations with Gate 9.2 inspired by GateContrib/imaging/ComptonCamera_TODO_GND (version of Oct. 2024, commit 13364d0e1757b864d1d3d887e9aae6228cf5ff96).

Pros:
- X-ray fluorescence is transported (not the case with Gate 10.0.1)

Cons:
- Problems with grid discretization module (gridDiscretization): does not work with single layer camera (Singles
  are only produced in scatterer and coincidences are not produced at all...
- Problems with ideal adder module (adderComptPhotIdeal): see below and in actor.mac

Starting from Gate 9.3 digitization changed and code would not work.

I added several utility scripts in subdirectory 'tools'.

To simulate perfect cones (e.g. to check their intersections with a point source):
- use adderComptPhotIdeal digitizer module
- use emstandard physics list to disable doppler broadening
- leave default cuts (1mm) to avoid fluorescence.

